==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|ἀντί||tr=anti|lang=grc|against}} + {{term|θέσις||tr=thesis|lang=grc|position}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ænˈtɪ.θə.sɪs/}}
* {{audio|en-us-antithesis.ogg|Audio (US)}}

{{examples-right|sense=rhetoric|examples=[[w:Abraham Lincoln|Abraham Lincoln]], ''[[s:Gettysburg Address|Gettysburg Address]]'' (1863)<br>The world will little note, nor long remember what we say here, but it can never forget what they did here.}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|antitheses}}

# A [[proposition]] that is the [[diametric]] [[opposite]] of some other proposition.
# {{rhetoric}} A device by which two contrasting ideas are [[juxtaposed]] in [[parallel]] form.

====Related terms====
* [[antithetical]]

